<div class=\"item-topics\">\n   584→                        <span class=\"topic\">SQLite</span>\n   585→                        <span class=\"topic\">scaling</span>\n   586→                        <span class=\"topic\">Go</span>\n   587→                    </div>\n   588→                </div>\n   589→\n   590→                <div class=\"item\">\n   591→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   592→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.21816\" target=\"_blank\">\n   593→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n   594→                            Tool Attention Is All You Need\n   595→                        </a>\n   596→                    </div>\n   597→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   598→                        Paper proposing 'Tool Attention' mechanism with dynamic tool gating and lazy schema loading to eliminate the MCP/tools tax in scalable agentic workflows.\n   599→                    </div>\n   600→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Anuj Sadani, Deepak Kumar</div>\n   601→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   602→                        <span class=\"topic\">agentic workflows</span>\n   603→                        <span class=\"topic\">tool use</span>\n   604→                        <span class=\"topic\">MCP</span>\n   605→                    </div>\n   606→                </div>\n   607→\n   608→                <div class=\"item\">\n   609→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   610→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.21910\" target=\"_blank\">\n   611→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n   612→                            Agentic AI for Science Automation\n   613→                        </a>\n   614→                    </div>\n   615→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   616→                        Paper exploring leveraging agentic AI to automate scientific workflows from research question to execution, potentially transforming how scientists conduct research.\n   617→                    </div>\n   618→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Bartosz Balis et al.</div>\n   619→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   620→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI agents</span>\n   621→                        <span class=\"topic\">scientific automation</span>\n   622→                    </div>\n   623→                </div>\n   624→\n   625→                <div class=\"item\">\n   626→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   627→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.21571\" target=\"_blank\">\n   628→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n   629→                            Separable Expert Architecture for LLM Personalization\n   630→                        </a>\n   631→                    </div>\n   632→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   633→                        Paper proposing a separable expert architecture for privacy-preserving LLM personalization via composable adapters and deletable user proxies.\n   634→                    </div>\n   635→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Chris Schneider et al.</div>\n   636→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   637→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM personalization</span>\n   638→                        <span class=\"topic\">privacy</span>\n   639→                    </div>\n   640→                </div>\n   641→\n   642→                <div class=\"item\">\n   643→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   644→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.21764\" target=\"_blank\">\n   645→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n   646→                            Thinking with Reasoning Skills: Fewer Tokens\n   647→                        </a>\n   648→                    </div>\n   649→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   650→                        Paper proposing methods to achieve higher accuracy with fewer tokens by focusing on reasoning skills, suggesting efficiency improvements in LLM inference.\n   651→                    </div>\n   652→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Guangxiang Zhao et al.</div>\n   653→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   654→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM efficiency</span>\n   655→                        <span class=\"topic\">reasoning</span>\n   656→                    </div>\n   657→                </div>\n   658→\n   659→                <div class=\"item\">\n   660→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   661→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/23/gpt-5.5/\" target=\"_blank\">\n   662→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-opinion\"></span>\n   663→                            GPT-5.5 available in OpenAI Codex\n   664→                        </a>\n   665→                    </div>\n   666→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   667→                        GPT-5.5 is out, available in OpenAI Codex and rolling out to paid ChatGPT subscribers. Simon found it fast, effective and highly capable.\n   668→                    </div>\n   669→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   670→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   671→                        <span class=\"topic\">OpenAI</span>\n   672→                        <span class=\"topic\">GPT-5.5</span>\n   673→                        <span class=\"topic\">coding agents</span>\n   674→                    </div>\n   675→                </div>\n   676→\n   677→                <div class=\"item\">\n   678→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   679→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/23/liteparse-web/\" target=\"_blank\">\n   680→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-tutorial\"></span>\n   681→                            LiteParse for the web: PDF text extraction\n   682→                        </a>\n   683→                    </div>\n   684→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   685→                        Simon ported LlamaIndex's LiteParse PDF extraction to run entirely in the browser, enabling client-side PDF text extraction without server.\n   686→                    </div>\n   687→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   688→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   689→                        <span class=\"topic\">PDF parsing</span>\n   690→                        <span class=\"topic\">browser-based AI</span>\n   691→                    </div>\n   692→                </div>\n   693→\n   694→                <div class=\"item\">\n   695→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   696→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/qwen3.6-27b/\" target=\"_blank\">\n   697→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n   698→                            Qwen3.6-27B: Flagship-Level Coding\n   699→                        </a>\n   700→                    </div>\n   701→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   702→                        Qwen released a 27B dense model claiming flagship-level agentic coding performance, surpassing their previous 397B MoE model.\n   703→                    </div>\n   704→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   705→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   706→                        <span class=\"topic\">open-source LLM</span>\n   707→                        <span class=\"topic\">local LLM</span>\n   708→                        <span class=\"topic\">coding agents</span>\n   709→                    </div>\n   710→                </div>\n   711→\n   712→                <div class=\"item\">\n   713→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   714→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/github-copilot-pricing/\" target=\"_blank\">\n   715→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-opinion\"></span>\n   716→                            GitHub Copilot pricing changes\n   717→                        </a>\n   718→                    </div>\n   719→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   720→                        GitHub changed Copilot Individual plans: tightening usage limits, pausing signups, restricting Opus 4.7 to Pro+ plan.\n   721→                    </div>\n   722→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   723→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   724→                        <span class=\"topic\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n   725→                        <span class=\"topic\">pricing</span>\n   726→                        <span class=\"topic\">coding agents</span>\n   727→                    </div>\n   728→                </div>\n   729→\n   730→                <div class=\"item\">\n   731→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   732→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/firefox-mythos/\" target=\"_blank\">\n   733→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n   734→                            Firefox 150: Claude found 271 vulnerabilities\n   735→                        </a>\n   736→                    </div>\n   737→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   738→                        Mozilla applied Claude Mythos Preview to Firefox and found/fixed 271 vulnerabilities in Firefox 150. Shows AI's potential for security work.\n   739→                    </div>\n   740→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   741→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   742→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI security</span>\n   743→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude</span>\n   744→                        <span class=\"topic\">Mozilla Firefox</span>\n   745→                    </div>\n   746→                </div>\n   747→\n   748→                <div class=\"item\">\n   749→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   750→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/claude-code-100/\" target=\"_blank\">\n   751→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-opinion\"></span>\n   752→                            Claude Code $100/month pricing confusion\n   753→                        </a>\n   754→                    </div>\n   755→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   756→                        Anthropic quietly updated pricing page to show $100/month plan, then reverted. Simon analyzes the confusion around Claude Code pricing.\n   757→                    </div>\n   758→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   759→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   760→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude</span>\n   761→                        <span class=\"topic\">pricing</span>\n   762→                        <span class=\"topic\">coding agents</span>\n   763→                    </div>\n   764→                </div>\n   765→\n   766→                <div class=\"item\">\n   767→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   768→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/21/chatgpt-images-2/\" target=\"_blank\">\n   769→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n   770→                            ChatGPT Images 2.0: GPT-3 to GPT-5 level leap\n   771→                        </a>\n   772→                    </div>\n   773→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   774→                        OpenAI released ChatGPT Images 2.0. Sam Altman claimed the leap from gpt-image-1 to gpt-image-2 is equivalent to jumping from GPT-3 to GPT-5.\n   775→                    </div>\n   776→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   777→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   778→                        <span class=\"topic\">OpenAI</span>\n   779→                        <span class=\"topic\">image generation</span>\n   780→                        <span class=\"topic\">GPT-5</span>\n   781→                    </div>\n   782→                </div>\n   783→\n   784→                <div class=\"item\">\n   785→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   786→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/21/less-human-ai/\" target=\"_blank\">\n   787→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-opinion\"></span>\n   788→                            Less human AI agents, please\n   789→                        </a>\n   790→                    </div>\n   791→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   792→                        Andreas Påhlsson-Notini argues current AI agents are too human in the wrong ways—lacking stringency, patience, focus.\n   793→                    </div>\n   794→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Andreas Påhlsson-Notini</div>\n   795→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   796→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI agents</span>\n   797→                        <span class=\"topic\">prompt engineering</span>\n   798→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI reliability</span>\n   799→                    </div>\n   800→                </div>\n   801→\n   802→                <div class=\"item\">\n   803→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   804→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/20/claude-token-counter/\" target=\"_blank\">\n   805→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-technical\"></span>\n   806→                            Claude Opus 4.7 tokenizer increases 1.46x\n   807→                        </a>\n   808→                    </div>\n   809→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   810→                        Simon built a token counter comparison tool and found Opus 4.7's new tokenizer uses 1.46x more tokens than 4.6 for the same text.\n   811→                    </div>\n   812→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   813→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   814→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude</span>\n   815→                        <span class=\"topic\">tokenization</span>\n   816→                        <span class=\"topic\">pricing</span>\n   817→                    </div>\n   818→                </div>\n   819→\n   820→                <div class=\"item\">\n   821→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   822→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/19/headless-everything/\" target=\"_blank\">\n   823→                            <span class=\"type-indicator type-opinion\"></span>\n   824→                            Headless everything for personal AI\n   825→                        </a>\n   826→                    </div>\n   827→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   828→                        Matt Webb and Marc Benioff predict headless services will become common as personal AIs interact via APIs rather than GUIs.\n   829→                    </div>\n   830→                    <div class=\"item-author\">Simon Willison</div>\n   831→                    <div class=\"item-topics\">\n   832→                        <span class=\"topic\">APIs</span>\n   833→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI agents</span>\n   834→                        <span class=\"topic\">SaaS pricing</span>\n   835→                    </div>\n   836→                </div>\n   837